sequenceDiagram
    participant CLI as CLI<br/>(run-composite)
    participant CPR as CompositePipelineRunner
    participant FSM as FSMStateHelperService
    participant Seed as PipelineRunner<br/>(chembl_publication)
    participant KE as KeyExtractorService
    participant EC as EnrichmentCoordinator
    participant PM as PipelineRunner<br/>(pubmed_publication)
    participant CR as PipelineRunner<br/>(crossref_publication)
    participant OA as PipelineRunner<br/>(openalex_publication)
    participant SS as PipelineRunner<br/>(semanticscholar_publication)
    participant MS as MergeService
    participant Alias as publication_aliases<br/>(compat registry)
    participant GW as GoldWriter

    CLI->>CPR: run(composite="publication")

    Note over CPR,FSM: Default composition assembly still injects the legacy FSM adapter path.
    Note over CPR,FSM: Phase 1: Seed pipeline
    CPR->>FSM: transition(NOT_STARTED → SEED_RUNNING)
    CPR->>Seed: run() — extract ChEMBL publications
    Seed-->>CPR: SeedResult(records=N, silver_path)
    CPR->>FSM: transition(SEED_RUNNING → SEED_COMPLETED)

    Note over CPR,KE: Phase 2: Key Extraction
    CPR->>KE: extract_keys(silver_path, join_keys=["doi","pmid","title"])
    KE-->>CPR: keys_df (doi, pmid, title columns)

    Note over CPR,SS: Phase 3: Fan-out enrichment via asyncio.gather(return_exceptions=True)
    Note over CPR,SS: All publication enrichers are optional in current config.<br/>Failures are collected and execution continues.
    CPR->>FSM: transition(SEED_COMPLETED → ENRICHING)
    CPR->>EC: run_enrichers(keys_df)

    par PubMed enrichment
        EC->>PM: run(filter_keys=pmid_list)
        PM-->>EC: EnrichmentResult(status=COMPLETED, records=M1)
    and CrossRef enrichment
        EC->>CR: run(filter_keys=doi_list)
        CR-->>EC: EnrichmentResult(status=COMPLETED, records=M2)
    and OpenAlex enrichment
        EC->>OA: run(filter_keys=doi_list)
        OA-->>EC: EnrichmentResult(status=COMPLETED, records=M3)
    and Semantic Scholar enrichment
        EC->>SS: run(filter_keys=doi_list)
        SS-->>EC: EnrichmentResult(status=PARTIAL, records=M4)
    end

    EC-->>CPR: enrichment_results[4]
    CPR->>FSM: transition(ENRICHING → ENRICHMENT_COMPLETED)

    Note over CPR,GW: Phase 4: Merge → Gold
    CPR->>FSM: transition(ENRICHMENT_COMPLETED → MERGING)
    CPR->>MS: merge(seed_silver, enricher_silvers)

    Note over MS: Step 4a: Read Silver tables
    MS->>MS: _read_silver_tables()<br/>DeltaReader for each source

    Note over MS: Step 4b: Join on DOI / PMID / title
    MS->>MS: _resolve_composite_join_keys()<br/>DOI/PMID matching + title fallback

    Note over MS,Alias: Step 4c: Preserve provider-qualified columns and apply field_priorities
    MS->>Alias: read legacy publication aliases<br/>cutoff=2026-06-30
    Alias-->>MS: publication_doi / publication_pmid / page_* aliases
    MS->>MS: _resolve_conflicts()<br/>field_priorities + preserve_all_sources

    Note over MS: Step 4d: Validate & write Gold
    MS->>GW: write_gold(merged_df)
    GW-->>MS: MergeResult(records=K, conflicts_resolved=C)

    MS-->>CPR: MergeResult
    CPR->>FSM: transition(MERGING → COMPLETED)
    CPR-->>CLI: CompositeResult(state=COMPLETED)
